SOURCE LAYOUT

  lib/Tk/  Perl modules
  src/     C, header and XS sources
  t/       Automated tests and GUI integration tests
  eg/      Runnable examples (.pl) and shared demo helper
  doc/     Screenshots and supplementary documentation

With Strawberry Perl on Windows, use gmake instead of make.
The GUI tests require a graphical desktop.

CLEANING THE BUILD

    gmake clean

Removes compiled and generated files, and renames Makefile to Makefile.old.
To remove the generated makefile as well, run realclean directly instead:

    gmake realclean

If clean has already been run, use:

    gmake -f Makefile.old realclean

Makefile.PL and myConfig are source files and must remain. To build again:

    perl Makefile.PL
    gmake

Use make instead of gmake where appropriate for your Perl installation.
